# Vercel CLI project link (created by `vercel` deploys) — never commit
.vercel/

# Licensed CraftPix art. The licence permits shipping it inside a deployed game and forbids a PUBLIC repo
# of the raw files, so it is ignored HERE and committed to the private deploy repo instead (see Dockerfile).
# `assets/*` rather than `assets/` so one placeholder can be re-included: it keeps the directory present in
# this tree, which is what makes the Dockerfile's `COPY assets/` valid in both repos.
#
# ⚠️ ADDING A NEW SPRITE? IT WILL NOT REACH THE DEPLOY UNTIL YOU COPY IT ACROSS.
# Your new PNG is ignored here (that is the point), and the private deploy repo carries a CURATED
# subset — only the 324 files the game was measured to load — so a code-only sync leaves it behind.
# The deploy will then 404 that file SILENTLY, because every image loader has an onerror fallback.
#     cp <new>.png ~/ry-farms-deploy/assets/<same path>
#     cd ~/ry-farms-deploy && git fetch public && git merge public/main && git add -f assets && git commit
# Full recipe, including how the 324 was measured: DEPLOY.md in ~/ry-farms-deploy.
#
assets/*
!assets/.placeholder.png

# local LLM key for the expressive channel (server.mjs) - NEVER commit
.env

# SuperMemory local self-hosted store (encrypted data + embedding models)
.supermemory/

# 1-bit icon reference pack (browsed in component-library/index.html) — NOT a runtime
# dependency of the game; 1.6k reference PNGs that don't belong in the shipped repo
component-library/

# personal Claude Code skill/config files — never belong in the project repo
